    "question_id": "qst_0006",
    "answer": "The proposed canonical evaluation order is: (1) authoritative reachability DOWN, which yields FAILOVER unless no healthy fallback exists; (2) high-severity/fast 5xx error burn, which yields FAILOVER or PARTIAL_SHIFT depending on blast radius and destination capacity; (3) p99/p95 tail-latency burn, which starts with PARTIAL_SHIFT and escalates to FAILOVER only when sustained and corroborated; and (4) capacity exhaustion/hard gate, which yields HOLD plus load shedding and explicitly avoids shifting traffic into the constrained region. Reachability DOWN overrides hold-down, and 5xx burn wins over latency burn when both fire.",
