    "question_id": "qst_0210",
    "answer": "Compute `SS = 100 * sum_p(w_p * (failure_count_p / max(1,total_calls_p))) / sum_p(w_p)` for priority-weighted test-slice failure density; `LP = 10 * max(0, (median_latency_ms - latency_slo_ms) / latency_slo_ms)`, clipped at 30; and `DF = 50 * embedding_drift_score_95pct_quantile`, normalized against baseline drift. Then `DS = clamp(SS + LP + DF, 0, 100)`. Bands: `DS <= 15` means GO/proceed; `15 < DS <= 35` means CAUTION/slow to 10% and conduct targeted human review within four hours; `35 < DS <= 60` means HOLD/pause and run automated bisect plus focused probes; and `DS > 60` means ROLLBACK/revert automatically to the baseline and open an incident.",
